# =============================================================================
# Media Radical — environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and edit:
#
#     cp .env.example .env.local
#
# `.env.local` is git-ignored.
#
# This file lists ONLY what the code reads today. Nothing speculative, nothing
# for features that do not exist yet. If a variable is not in here, no code
# looks for it.
#
# The site runs with none of these set. Both have working defaults.
#
# Both are NEXT_PUBLIC_*, which means two things:
#   1. They are inlined into the JavaScript at BUILD time. Changing one on
#      Render needs a redeploy, not a restart.
#   2. They are readable by every visitor in the page source, so neither can
#      ever hold a secret. The site is a static export with no server, so
#      there is nowhere to keep a secret anyway. Anything requiring an API key
#      means moving back to a Web Service.
#
# When you add a variable: add it here with a comment, and note it in
# README.md and DONE.md. See CLAUDE.md.
# =============================================================================


# --- Public origin ------------------------------------------------------------
# Absolute origin of this deployment, no trailing slash.
#
# Read by: data/site.ts, which feeds app/layout.tsx (metadataBase), the
# canonical link, app/sitemap.ts, app/robots.ts and every JSON-LD @id in
# utils/schema.ts.
#
# Unset locally it defaults to http://localhost:3000, so development needs no
# .env file.
#
# Unset on Render the build FAILS ON PURPOSE. It used to fall back to the
# production URL, which caused a real incident: the staging site deployed with
# this unset, did not fail, and served
# <link rel="canonical" href="https://mediaradical.in"> plus a sitemap pointing
# at production. A staging site claiming to be production is how a domain gets
# deduplicated out of a search index, and it stays invisible until it has
# already done damage. A failed build is the cheaper outcome.
#
#   Local:      http://localhost:3000   (automatic, nothing to set)
#   Staging:    https://mediaradical.onrender.com
#   Production: https://mediaradical.in
#
# On Render this is declared in render.yaml with `sync: false`, so it is set in
# the dashboard per service rather than committed here.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000


# --- Newsletter endpoint ------------------------------------------------------
# Where components/layout/FooterNewsletter.tsx posts the address. Any endpoint
# accepting a POST works: a form relay such as FormSubmit or Formspree, or a
# mailing-list provider's own URL.
#
# Unset is a supported state, not a broken one. The form still validates, then
# says signup is not connected and points at the contact address. It never
# thanks someone for a subscription that went nowhere.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_NEWSLETTER_ENDPOINT=https://formsubmit.co/ajax/your-address


# =============================================================================
# Set by the platform, not by you
#
# RENDER  Render sets this to "true" on every service. data/site.ts reads it to
#         tell a real deployment apart from someone running `npm run build`
#         locally, which is what decides whether a missing NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL
#         fails the build or quietly falls back to localhost. Do not set it by
#         hand: doing so locally will make your own builds fail.
# =============================================================================
